{
  "format": "synthyboy-overlay-layout",
  "version": 4,
  "comment": "Source of the numbers the overlay build shares between the skin (skin/TUI.json) and the plugin (shell-mpc/overlay/overlay_layout.h, hand-maintained, no generator). A VIEW is a region of a tab (rectangle in the coordinates of the tab, 1280 x 628, which starts at screen y tabOriginY) with a pair of marker squares of colours that no other view uses: the plugin finds which view is on screen by the markers alone. Opaque views get a dark picture over their region (the skin keeps its own pictures underneath); the transparent one covers only its two marker squares with the colour `cover`. Colours are 6 hex digits RRGGBB. INSTANCE: which plugin instance's page is on screen. Every plugin instance owns a slot 0..15 (assigned when it is created, freed when it closes); the display-only parameter \"Overlay Instance\" (the last parameter of the list) carries frame number slot + 1 of a film strip of `frames` frames (value = frame / 32), and the skin draws a tiny image bound to it inside every view's region, next to the markers (per view: `instance`). The pixel colour read from the primary framebuffer tells the plugin which instance the host drew the page of: frame 0 and the unused frames are `blank` (nothing reported yet), frame 17 is `none` (an instance beyond the 16 slots), frames 1 .. 16 are `slots`. The colours must differ from every marker colour and from one another by more than the detector's tolerance. PAGES: a view whose region is the whole tab (kinds play, filterui, envui, lfoui, oscui, macros, mixer, fx, mod, master, voice) is a page the plugin draws entirely; the skin hides the host widgets of that tab while the page is up. METERROW: the row of the 32 native Meter widgets of the Macros tab (the geometry of the spectrum of the plugin's Macros page; the host Meters that were drawn there are gone).",
  "screen": {
    "width": 1280,
    "height": 800
  },
  "tabOriginY": 110,
